  "enhanced_information": "The clinical presentation of the 9-month-old girl, including fever, irritability, ear discharge, and physical examination findings of erythema and tenderness in the right postauricular region, along with a bulging and cloudy tympanic membrane with pus, strongly suggests acute otitis media, potentially complicated by mastoiditis. The elevated leukocyte count and neutrophil percentage further indicate a bacterial infection. According to standard medical consensus, oral amoxicillin is the first-line treatment for acute otitis media in children, especially when there are signs of severe infection or complications like mastoiditis. Other options, such as topical ciprofloxacin, nasal drops, CT scans, or aspirin, are not appropriate first-line treatments in this scenario. Therefore, the most appropriate next step in management is oral amoxicillin therapy.",
